# Section title gap

The space from a section heading to its first content is **`--shell-title-gap`** (`--space-4`, 16px) in [`design-system/tokens.css`](design-system/tokens.css).

Applies to lobby headings (`Providers`, `Recent bets`, `Sponsors`, `Brand Ambassador`, `RECENT PAYOUT`), `.section__head`, footer column titles, and any new page section.

```css
/* BAD — one-off gap */
.recent-payout-header { margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }
.trust-sponsor .home-section__title { margin-bottom: 0; }

/* GOOD */
.home-section__title,
.recent-payout-header { margin-bottom: var(--shell-title-gap); }
```

Do not zero a title margin and rely on a parent `gap` — that makes Sponsors/Ambassador drift from Providers. If the parent already has `gap`, subtract it: `margin-bottom: calc(var(--shell-title-gap) - var(--space-N))`.

To change the rhythm everywhere, edit **`--shell-title-gap` only**. Inner stacks (name → bio → followers) stay `--space-3`. Section-to-section remains `--shell-section-gap`.
